{
  "title": { "en": "Squash it into one row" },
  "short": { "en": "The rewrite direction is the meaning" },
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Look closely at the knapsack table: each row only uses <b>the row above</b>. So why keep the whole table? Keep just one row, and rewrite it in place for each item."
      },
      "fig": {
        "scene": {
          "cells": [
            { "id": "ax0", "x": 0, "y": -38, "w": 44, "h": 26, "value": 0, "cls": "axis" },
            { "id": "ax1", "x": 52, "y": -38, "w": 44, "h": 26, "value": 1, "cls": "axis" },
            { "id": "ax2", "x": 104, "y": -38, "w": 44, "h": 26, "value": 2, "cls": "axis" },
            { "id": "ax3", "x": 156, "y": -38, "w": 44, "h": 26, "value": 3, "cls": "axis" },
            { "id": "0,0", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "dimc" },
            { "id": "0,1", "x": 52, "y": 0, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "dimc" },
            { "id": "0,2", "x": 104, "y": 0, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "dimc" },
            { "id": "0,3", "x": 156, "y": 0, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "dimc" },
            { "id": "1,0", "x": 0, "y": 52, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "1,1", "x": 52, "y": 52, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "1,2", "x": 104, "y": 52, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 3, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "1,3", "x": 156, "y": 52, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 3, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "2,0", "x": 0, "y": 104, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 0, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "2,1", "x": 52, "y": 104, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 2, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "2,2", "x": 104, "y": 104, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 3, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "2,3", "x": 156, "y": 104, "w": 44, "h": 44, "value": 5, "cls": "lit" }
          ],
          "edges": [
            { "a": "1,3", "b": "2,3", "cls": "dim", "bend": 0, "off": 0 },
            { "a": "1,2", "b": "2,3", "cls": "dim", "bend": 0, "off": 0 }
          ],
          "texts": [
            { "x": -32, "y": -33, "t": { "en": "capacity" }, "anchor": "end" },
            { "x": -32, "y": 5, "t": { "en": "nothing" }, "anchor": "end" },
            { "x": -32, "y": 57, "t": { "en": "camera 2kg · 3" }, "anchor": "end" },
            { "x": -32, "y": 109, "t": { "en": "bottle 1kg · 2" }, "anchor": "end" }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Rewriting in place carries a risk: rewriting dp[w] reads dp[w − weight]. If that cell <b>has already been rewritten this round</b>, what you read is a value where the item “has already been taken”."
      },
      "fig": {
        "scene": {
          "cells": [
            { "id": "d0", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 46, "h": 46, "value": 0, "corner": 0, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "d1", "x": 56, "y": 0, "w": 46, "h": 46, "value": 2, "corner": 1, "cls": "bad" },
            { "id": "d2", "x": 112, "y": 0, "w": 46, "h": 46, "value": 4, "corner": 2, "cls": "lit" },
            { "id": "d3", "x": 168, "y": 0, "w": 46, "h": 46, "value": "?", "corner": 3, "cls": "hot" },
            { "id": "d4", "x": 224, "y": 0, "w": 46, "h": 46, "corner": 4 }
          ],
          "edges": [{ "a": "d1", "b": "d3", "cls": "bad", "bend": -36, "off": 0 }]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "This level has two kinds of backpack: one where <b>each item can be taken at most once</b>, and one where <b>each item can be taken many times</b> (like a shop with plenty of everything). The board isn’t hard: new dp[w] = max(old dp[w], dp[w − weight] + value). The red frame dp[w] in the view is where the new value is written, and clicking it in the view reads the old value before it is rewritten; dp[w − weight] is what the telescopic arm reaches."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The real trick is the machine’s <wiki-ref to=\"dirs\"></wiki-ref>: when each item can be taken at most once, it rewrites <b>right to left</b>; when each item can be taken many times, it rewrites <b>left to right</b>. Why does the same circuit board give different answers when only the direction changes?"
      }
    }
  ],
  "mission": {
    "goal": {
      "en": "In one kind of backpack each item can be taken at most once; in the other, many times. Either way, the total weight can’t exceed the capacity. Build the circuit so that all four tests come out right."
    },
    "how": {
      "en": "Yellow is the cell being rewritten; red means a value rewritten earlier this round was read."
    }
  },
  "robot": "reach",
  "debrief": {
    "title": { "en": "Direction is meaning" },
    "body": [
      {
        "en": "Rewriting from right to left, dp[w − weight] hasn’t been touched by this item yet, so it reads an old value: <b>each item at most once</b>."
      },
      {
        "en": "Rewriting from left to right, dp[w − weight] may already include this item, and taking it again is just right: <b>each item as many times as you like</b>."
      },
      {
        "en": "The same circuit board, just a different direction, solves two different problems. Keeping only one row like this is called a <b>rolling array</b>, and it can squash a table thousands of rows tall into a single row."
      }
    ],
    "note": {
      "en": "One row rewritten in place: right to left, once each; left to right, unlimited."
    }
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "roll",
      "mode": "circuit",
      "naive": ["a = add(view.src, facts.value)", "cell <- a"],
      "diagnose": [
        {
          "when": { "not": { "all": [{ "uses": "old" }, { "uses": "src" }, { "uses": "value" }] } },
          "say": {
            "en": "The circuit board: new dp[w] = max(old dp[w], dp[w − weight] + value). All three need reading in: the old dp[w], dp[w − weight] and the item value."
          }
        }
      ],
      "after": "roll",
      "explain": "roll",
      "boardOpt": { "minScale": 0.66, "maxScale": 1.15 },
      "noTrace": true,
      "world": "roll",
      "facts": ["value"],
      "tests": [
        {
          "kind": "01",
          "W": 6,
          "items": [
            { "n": { "en": "cans" }, "w": 1, "v": 1 },
            { "n": { "en": "raincoat" }, "w": 3, "v": 4 },
            { "n": { "en": "blanket" }, "w": 4, "v": 5 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "inf",
          "W": 7,
          "items": [
            { "n": { "en": "apples" }, "w": 2, "v": 3 },
            { "n": { "en": "melons" }, "w": 3, "v": 5 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "01",
          "W": 7,
          "items": [
            { "n": { "en": "camera" }, "w": 3, "v": 4 },
            { "n": { "en": "bottle" }, "w": 4, "v": 5 },
            { "n": { "en": "snacks" }, "w": 2, "v": 3 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "inf",
          "W": 9,
          "items": [
            { "n": { "en": "flour" }, "w": 5, "v": 9 },
            { "n": { "en": "rice" }, "w": 3, "v": 5 },
            { "n": { "en": "sugar" }, "w": 2, "v": 3 }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expected": [6, 11, 9, 15],
      "solution": ["a = add(view.src, facts.value)", "m = mmax(view.old, a)", "cell <- m"],
      "dirs": { "01": "desc", "inf": "asc" }
    }
  ]
}
